      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test class has many unused data providers, helper methods, constants, and imports that are irrelevant to the single `@Test` method. I'll produce a focused, clean version.The `compile.sh` expects the file in the same directory. I need to write the test there instead.The improved test compiles successfully. The key understandability improvements made:\n\n1. **Removed dead code**: eliminated 6 unused data-provider methods (`data_badParse`, `data_withModifiedJulianDay`, `data_withNanoOfDay`, `data_plus`, `data_minus`, `data_toString`) and the `doTest_comparisons_UtcInstant` helper that were copied from a larger test class but had no connection to this test.\n2. **Pruned unused imports**: dropped `ByteArrayInputStream/OutputStream`, `ObjectInputStream/OutputStream`, `Serializable`, `DateTimeException`, `Duration`, `Instant`, `@Nullable`, `ParameterizedTest`, `MethodSource`, `EqualsTester`, `assertFalse`, `assertNotEquals`, and `assertThrows`.\n3. **Removed unused constants**: kept only `MJD_1972_12_31_LEAP`, `SECS_PER_DAY`, `NANOS_PER_SEC`, and `NANOS_PER_LEAP_DAY` — the four values actually needed.\n4. **Introduced a named local variable** `lastNanoOfLeapDay` to make the intent of `NANOS_PER_LEAP_DAY - 1` explicit at the call site.\n5. **Added a Javadoc comment** on the test method explaining the leap-second scenario and why `isLeapSecond()` is expected to return `true`."
